{
  "schema": "aurie.charm.taxonomy/1",
  "_readme": [
    "HAND-AUTHORED editorial product metadata. The charm processor NEVER",
    "writes this file — charms.json is processing output (provenance,",
    "attachment, thumbnails); THIS file is product truth (what a charm",
    "means, where it can be worn, how it can be earned).",
    "generate_charm_catalog.py merges the two into the runtime catalog",
    "(CharmCatalog.generated.swift). Edit here, then re-run the generator.",
    "Three concepts stay independent and multi-valued: placements (where",
    "worn), categories (what it represents), acquisitionSources (how it",
    "can be earned). Birth triggers are a SEPARATE table: a trigger maps",
    "recognition labels to ONE charm — categories never unlock anything.",
    "The taxonomy may reference charms before their assets exist and may",
    "keep working after a library asset is removed; it is deliberately",
    "not limited to current AurieCharmLibrary contents."
  ],
